#
# Owner: the agent editing ms2_ue.cpp.  coordinator asked for the exact unified diff
# instead of a concurrent edit, because two agents writing that file at once is how
# the tree got broken before.  Everything else in this brief is already in the tree;
# this is the only change that still has to be merged by hand.
#
# WHAT IT FIXES (verified, not guessed)
# -------------------------------------
# native\src\coop_progress.cpp read store B through ue::MapForEach(), which takes the
# map geometry from the UE4 layout of FMapProperty:
#
#     kOffMapLayoutK = 0x70   FScriptMapLayout::KeyOffset   (int32)
#     kOffMapLayoutV = 0x74   FScriptMapLayout::ValueOffset (int32)
#     kOffMapKeyProp = 0x78   FMapProperty::KeyProp
#     kOffMapValProp = 0x80   FMapProperty::ValueProp
#
# This build's SDK -- research\raw\Dumper7\SDK\Basic.hpp, "Predefined struct
# FMapProperty // 0x0010 (0x0080 - 0x0070)" -- says otherwise:
#
#     class FMapProperty final : public FProperty
#     {
#         class FProperty* KeyProperty;      // 0x0070(0x0008)(NOT AUTO-GENERATED PROPERTY)
#         class FProperty* ValueProperty;    // 0x0078(0x0008)(NOT AUTO-GENERATED PROPERTY)
#     };
#
# i.e. FMapProperty is 0x80 bytes and there is NO FScriptMapLayout member (UE5
# derives the pair offsets from the two properties).  Consequence in the current
# code: the int32 halves of the KeyProperty POINTER are read as keyOff/valueOff, and
# the "ValueProperty" is then read from the 8 bytes AFTER the property object (past
# its end).  That either fails PlausiblePtr or yields a nonsense ElementSize, so
# ReadMapInfo() returns false and MapForEach() returns false SILENTLY for every map
# in the game.
#
# Observed symptom (two-client run, sync.txt on both clients):
#       wp=b:0/0+0!0 q:13/13+0!0 d:104/0+0!0
#                          ^^^ store B: 0 local entries, 0 peer entries
# while the Lua build of the same run printed `b:5/5`.  The `q:` half shows the
# non-map sources (tags/quests/layers) working, which is exactly what a broken map
# walk looks like: everything that does not need a TMap still works.
#
# WHY THE PATCH IS SHAPED THIS WAY
# --------------------------------
# * KeyProperty 0x70 / ValueProperty 0x78 -- straight from the SDK above.
# * No MapLayout read at all; the value offset inside TPair<Key,Value> is derived
#   from the two ElementSizes (DerivedValueOffset).  Checked against every map this
#   mod touches:
#       TMap<FName,int32>            key 8  value  4 -> value@8   pair 12 -> stride 20
#       TMap<FName,bool>             key 8  value  1 -> value@8   pair 12 -> stride 20
#       TMap<FString,int32>          key16  value  4 -> value@16  pair 20 -> stride 24
#       TMap<FName,FSpartaMapInt>    key 8  value 80 -> value@8   pair 88 -> stride 96
#       TMap<FName,UObject*>         key 8  value  8 -> value@8   pair 16 -> stride 24
#   (all sizes from the same SDK: FSpartaMapInt/Bool are 0x0050 with `Map` at 0x0000)
# * MapFindKey() (used by MapAddNameInt/MapAddStrInt, i.e. every quest-map write) had
#   the same wrong offsets; it is fixed the same way.
# * The silent failure is made visible: one ms2::Logf() the first 4 times ReadMapInfo
#   refuses a property, with the geometry it used.  If it still fails after this
#   patch the log names the property and the numbers instead of the caller guessing.
# * MapForEachRaw() is untouched: it never reads a property (caller supplies the
#   sizes), which is why coop_progress.cpp can already work with ue::MapForEachRaw
#   alone -- see WalkMapProp()/ScanSaveMap() there.  Merging this patch makes the
#   property-based form correct too, which is what every other module uses.
#
# VERIFICATION STATUS
# -------------------
# * All five hunks were generated against the working tree's ms2_ue.cpp and then
#   re-checked with `git apply --check` against that file as it stands now: every
#   hunk applies (with a +14 line offset, because that file is being edited in
#   parallel -- line numbers moved, the context did not).
# * The patched copy compiles warning-free with the project's own flags
#   (cl /c /O2 /W3 /std:c++20 /permissive- ...), so the hunks are syntactically and
#   type-wise sound against the current file, not only against my snapshot.
# * The element-stride arithmetic is the same as MapForEachRaw's, which is
#   independent of FMapProperty, so store B is exercisable today without this patch.
# * Not verified against live memory (no game run available): the TBitArray layout
#   the walker assumes for AllocationFlags (ptr@0x10, num@0x18, NumBits@0x20) is
#   unchanged by this patch.  If it is wrong the walker falls back to "the key must
#   decode as a real FName/FString", which is why a wrong flags offset loses no rows.
#
